  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` events now carry `amountCents` and `createdAt` as well as the old `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The 39 unit tests pass and `npm run arch` finds no new violations. I didn't run `npm run typecheck`, but `npm test` compiles the source with `tsc`.\n\n- **Change:** in `src/core/events.ts`, `createdAt` has the same value as `placedAt`, and `amountCents` has the same value as `totalCents`. The old names are still there, so current consumers keep working.\n- **Schema version:** I left `schemaVersion` at 3, because adding fields doesn't break consumers that ignore fields they don't know. A consumer that validates events strictly and rejects unknown fields would break. Let me know if you want a bump to 4 anyway.\n- **Test:** I updated the exact-match assertion in `test/app.test.ts` to include the two new fields.\n- **HTTP API:** the `POST /orders` response still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because you only asked about the event.\n- **Next step:** once the consumers have moved to the new names, you can retire the old fields in a later schema version.",
